menu "MZ CMT transport"
config MZ_CAPTURE_GPIO_FALLBACK
    bool "Use diagnostic GPIO/GPTimer capture fallback"
    default n
    help
        Default capture uses MCPWM hardware-latched edge timestamps.
        Enable only for diagnostics/comparison with the old GPIO ISR path.
config MZ_TX_GPTIMER_FALLBACK
    bool "Use diagnostic GPTimer TX fallback"
    default n
    help
        Default TX uses RMT DMA with one continuous encoder transaction.
        This option retains the older per-interval GPTimer for comparison.
config MZ_RX_PCNT_GUARD
    bool "Independent PCNT WRITE edge diagnostic"
    default n
    help
        Counts both GPIO5 edges independently of MCPWM with no glitch filter.
        Epoch boundary uncertainty is reported, not treated as proven loss.
        Enable after board timing checks; no extra pin or wire is required.
endmenu
